* /**
*  * @file GIT.ECHO
*  * @version 1.0
*  */
* GIT.ECHO(text) — print git-object output, one @AM-separated line per PRINT.
*
* Replaces GITUDT.SHOW, which had to OSREAD the CallC message file because
* CallC cannot marshal a string return.  That file is an artefact of one
* transport, so it now lives behind GIT.OBJ; every caller has the text in hand
* and only needs it printed.  Nothing here is platform-specific.
      SUBROUTINE GIT.ECHO(TEXT)
      IF TEXT # "" THEN
         AM = CHAR(254)
         NL = DCOUNT(TEXT, AM)
         FOR I = 1 TO NL
            PRINT TEXT<I>
         NEXT I
      END
      RETURN
      END
